From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:14:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: admit a connected scan while cleanup is only
 armed

The driver requests its cleanup when the association request completes, so
join_cleanup_requested is set throughout the data phase and the teardown only
starts at the data end. The connected scan's admission refused on that flag,
so every scan during a connection returned -EBUSY.

Refuse once the cleanup is done instead; join_data_ended already covers
the teardown.

Fixes the scan while connected. Part of the Wi-Fi daily-use plan, phase 4.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
index b77eb8ca4..344462754 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
@@ -986,7 +986,7 @@ static int mt6797_mac_hw_scan(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, struct ieee80211_vif *vif
 	 * reports it and the supplicant retries.
 	 */
 	online = mac->join_data_phase && !mac->join_data_ended &&
-		 mac->join_channel_released && mac->join_sta_active && !mac->join_cleanup_requested;
+		 mac->join_channel_released && mac->join_sta_active && !mac->join_cleanup_done;
 	if ((mac->scan_used && !online) || mac->scan_online || mac->scan_online_cancel) {
 		dev_info_ratelimited(wiphy_dev(hw->wiphy),
 				     "one-shot WLAN scan busy: used=%u data=%u ended=%u released=%u sta=%u cleanup=%u online=%u cancel=%u\n",
